Theorem 1. The logarithm has no global branch on the circle.

Three arcs, each a little more than a third of the circle.
On each arc the logarithm has a branch.
Going round, the branches disagree by one turn.

Cover the circle by U1, U2 and U3.
The transition on U1 and U2 is 0.
The transition on U2 and U3 is 0.
The transition on U3 and U1 is 1.

By gluing.

The value is zero.

WLOG.

The branches do not glue. The obstruction is on stderr.
It is the winding number.

QED.
